        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "L59h8",
          "name": "Behavior and accessibility heading",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Behavior to preserve",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "S8wTAg",
          "name": "Reading and action behavior",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Reading and focus order: global navigation → Study all questions → Start mock test → Edit date → groups in their original order. Each group action opens the existing group route and keeps the saved position. Its accessible name includes the group title.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "BbPiL",
          "name": "Progress behavior",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Show the exact contributing count and the nearest whole-number percentage for overall and group progress: Math.round(100 × contributing / total). Learning and Learned each contribute one question; Not started and Needs review contribute zero. Never display decimal percentages, including status-legend percentages. Examples: 1/310 → 0%, 2/310 → 1%, 50/310 → 16%. Segment proportions use exact status counts rather than rounded labels. Rounding may display 100% before every question contributes; the exact count and colors remain authoritative. Full green requires every question to be Learned.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "s7BXgT",
          "name": "First use behavior",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "First use: show 0% and 0 / 310 learning or learned inside the overall status ring. Its entire circumference is gray Not started; the legend shows 310 Not started and 0 for all other statuses. Group bars are fully gray Not started. No saved position: Study group. Active position: Continue group plus Continue at question {position} of {total}, using the saved one-based group position independently of progress. Completed pass: View completed group, even below 100%; no resume hint.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "G9ZZO",
          "name": "Responsive behavior",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Desktop: group identity, progress, and action columns. Tablet: group beside progress and action. Mobile: title and full description, then progress beside a compact 48 px study action. The resume hint sits immediately below the status bar within the progress column at every breakpoint. Stack progress and action when longer localized labels cannot fit. Coarse-pointer devices activate the study link from the entire group row. Bottom navigation meets the frame bottom and includes its safe-area spacing.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "XJdaS",
          "name": "Focus and loading behavior",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Actions have 48 px targets. Retain a visible focus ring in both themes; do not move focus when progress updates. Loading or unreadable local data follows the existing startup/recovery flow rather than displaying false zero progress. Date examples use Oct 3, 2026 with a planned test on Oct 8.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "g1hEzQ",
          "name": "Home first use · changed regions only",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "stroke": "$surface-raised",
          "strokeWidth": {
            "top": 1
          },
          "gap": 32,
          "padding": [
            24,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "XNDvH",
              "name": "First-use summary",
              "context": "Full-width progress region. Center chart and right-hand legend as a pair on desktop/tablet; place a compact two-column legend below the chart on mobile. Whole percentages use Math.round(100 × count / total). Exact counts determine segment angles. Ring order: Not started, Needs review, Learning, Learned. Legend items are accessible buttons: hover/focus highlights a matching slice; mouse click, touch tap, or keyboard activation toggles selected status. Keep exact counts and percentages readable. All green means every question Learned. See separate Legend interaction specification in the state library.",
              "width": 350,
              "fill": "$bg",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 16,
              "alignItems": "center",
              "children": [
