            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Aj5FO",
              "name": "First-use scope note",
              "fill": "$text-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "No answers yet. Start studying to track progress. Use the same Home layout and all 13 group rows; every action is Study group. These are the only changed regions.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "mDXHv",
          "name": "Cross-screen implementation contract",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Shared screen rules: use the Home palette, 8 px controls, 48 px primary actions and Inter typography. Main pages use 32 px desktop/tablet headings and 28 px mobile headings; German question prompts use 28 / 24 px. Supporting reading text is at least 14 px; 12 px is reserved for navigation, compact status and metadata. Preserve German source content in both interface languages.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ClY7Y",
          "name": "Modal and validation implementation contract",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Dialogs are viewport overlays: 520 px on desktop, viewport width minus 40 px on mobile. Initial focus is the safe action (Open question list, Stay in test, or Cancel), with a focus trap and Escape restoration. Date errors appear after blur or save, preserve the typed value, and leave the saved date unchanged. Import failure keeps local data untouched; submitting actions block duplicate activation.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "qKG9Y",
          "name": "Supportive feedback heading",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Supportive feedback · shared interaction contract",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-20",
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "t4TrPx",
          "name": "Study acknowledgment",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Study shows correctness through the selected-answer and correct-answer styling and icons, with the current learning-status badge. Do not render a Correct, Incorrect, or Learned notification, correction block, or milestone explanation. Announce new feedback once in a visually hidden polite live region: Correct, Incorrect, or Correct — now marked Learned. Preserve the session answer on back/forward navigation without announcing it again. Do not move focus, auto-advance, or delay controls. Mock-test review retains its visible answer feedback.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "kFrJ8",
          "name": "Translation and recovery",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "English Study translations remain alongside the German question and answer options when enabled. Do not repeat the correct-answer translation in a separate feedback notice. Failed results keep score, threshold, unanswered count and finish reason, then offer review guidance; use below only in stacked layouts. Passing results show Mock test passed, the actual score, a check and Well done. No real-test guarantee.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Z7DKm",
          "name": "Completion and repetition",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Completion acknowledges reaching the group’s end, not mastery or 100% progress. Keep the check beside the heading, separate from the exact progress fraction. Review starts another pass and preserves history. All added treatments are static; no sound, confetti, streaks, toasts or reduced-motion dependency. Retain keyboard focus, 48 px controls and wrapping copy.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "L5k8l",
          "name": "Localization wording",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "German interface labels: Im Lernen; Einstellungen; Lernsitzung abgeschlossen; Erneut üben. Combined progress counts read im Lernen oder gelernt (English: learning or learned). Headings omit trailing full stops; explanatory sentences retain normal punctuation. Group completion: Du hast das Ende dieser Gruppe erreicht. Correctness and Learned acknowledgments in Study are screen-reader announcements only.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "AAloB",
          "name": "Study help · expanded state reference",
          "context": "Default screens show this disclosure collapsed. Expanding adds this copy below its 44 px trigger; preserve focus, current answer and scroll access. German label: So funktioniert Lernen. German body: Beantworte jede Frage einmal pro Lernsitzung. Zurück und Weiter behalten deine Antworten und Rückmeldungen bei. Starte eine neue Lernsitzung oder öffne eine Frage unter Fortschritt, um erneut zu antworten. Frühere Versuche und gespeicherte Positionen bleiben erhalten.",
          "width": 700,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": "$spacing-8",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "yJsKf",
              "name": "How study works · expanded trigger",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "height": 44,
              "gap": "$spacing-8",
              "alignItems": "center",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "icon",
                  "id": "cGGcO",
                  "name": "Collapse study help",
                  "width": 18,
                  "height": 18,
                  "icon": "chevron-up",
                  "library": "lucide",
                  "fill": "$text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "UCTcS",
                  "name": "Expanded help label",
                  "fill": "$text",
                  "content": "How study works",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Z9WJ3i",
              "name": "Study help body",
              "fill": "$text-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Answer each question once per session. Previous and Next retain your answers and feedback. Start a new study session, or open a question from Progress, to answer again. Earlier attempts and saved positions remain.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "cOgTb",
          "name": "Distilled interface · shared behavior heading",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Distilled interface · shared behavior",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-20",
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "nz8G3",
          "name": "Status filters",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Progress has exclusive Question status and Mock tests tabs. Status filters use bank-wide counts. Question status lists all 13 groups; each expands independently and shows 10 matches, then 10 more per group action. Changing the filter resets each group to 10. Keep zero-match groups visible. Tab switches and question history preserve filters, expanded groups, revealed counts and position.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "nrR2c",
          "name": "Study and review order",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Study order: context and position → scope status bar (8 px below context) → learning-status badge → German prompt → Show English translation switch → translated prompt → image if present → choices → navigation → collapsed How study works. There is no visible feedback notification. Keep correctness icons and answer styling, and a visually hidden polite announcement for new answers. The status bar reflects current group or all-question totals and updates after answers. Below 1024 px, all app screens omit the brand header and its space, including on tablet. Tablet navigation starts at the top; desktop retains its sidebar header. German UI omits translation. Mobile bottom navigation remains fixed with scroll clearance.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "b3xBL",
          "name": "Backup and confirmations",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Settings groups Download backup, Backup file and its preview under Backup. Comparison contains seven rows: study attempts, completed tests, unfinished tests, planned date, interface language, study translation, appearance. Import opens Replace local data? before replacement. Reset progress and settings opens its own confirmation. Date input displays DD.MM.YYYY; Settings has no countdown. Typed past dates show an error while the saved date is retained. Successful import and reset output Backup imported. Your history and settings on this device have been replaced.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "xwtC2",
          "name": "Responsive and theme contract",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "All group descriptions and direct study paths remain visible. At widths or text sizes where progress and a study action cannot fit together, stack them in the same reading order. Keep 48 px group actions, 44 px translation/disclosure controls and visible focus rings. Count and percentage rules are unchanged. Use existing light/dark semantic colors; correctness and learning status retain text/icon cues.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "i0NcJ",
          "name": "Localization for added labels",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "How study works → So funktioniert Lernen; Backup → Datensicherung. Combined German filters use the existing app vocabulary: Alle, Nicht begonnen, Wiederholen, In Bearbeitung and Gelernt, with counts. No new learning statuses or calculation rules. The translation switch remains absent in German UI.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "G9sPE",
          "name": "German filter reference heading",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "German status filters · mobile width",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-16",
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "yluXg",
          "name": "German status filters · 350 px content width",
          "context": "Combined status summary and filters. Counts cover the entire question bank, independent of the selected filter. Keep All and all four statuses visible. First use: All 310, Not started 310, other counts 0. Expose selected state and counts in accessible names. Wrap controls in semantic order for German labels and narrow layouts; never truncate labels or reduce targets below 44 px.",
          "width": 350,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "WDAAq",
              "name": "Learning status filters row 1",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "gap": 8,
              "children": [
