          "type": "text",
          "id": "n9RQW",
          "name": "Design synchronization reference",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Study, Home, Settings and relevant shared notes synchronized to app commit 48e4dbd (UX improvements), 6 October 2026. Progress-page designs remain unchanged pending implementation. Example learner data and dates remain illustrative (base date 3 October 2026). Public pages are / and /en/; learner Home is /dashboard. Desktop Study and live Mock test use 50vw centered beside the sidebar. Settings and Cheat sheet designs now fill the main area like Progress (17 October 2026). Static frames do not verify runtime behavior.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "LHuJV",
          "name": "Overall status ring behavior",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "No visible overall-progress or status-legend headings. Retain an accessible chart name of Overall learning progress. Keep legend counts and percentages in consistent right-aligned columns close to the labels; on mobile, place the color dot to the left of one shared text stack, with the status label and count line aligned to the same left edge. On mobile, use a compact inline count · percentage line with content-sized values and 4 px gaps; do not right-align percentages or reserve numeric column widths. Overall progress layout: keep the chart and its right-hand legend centered together within the full-width region on desktop and tablet. On mobile, center the chart above a compact two-column legend. Preserve semantic status order and allow longer localized labels to wrap; expand legend items beyond their minimum height if needed. Ring segments run clockwise from 12 o’clock; group bars use the same left-to-right order: Not started (grey0), Needs review (danger), Learning (orange), Learned (success). Size every segment from exact status count / total. Do not add minimum segments or draw a segment for zero counts. Show whole percentages only, rounded to the nearest integer. Keep zero-count statuses and exact counts in the legend. Center shows (Learning + Learned) / total and its whole-number percentage. Full green requires all Learned. Loading/unreadable data follows existing recovery. Home example: first group = 25 Not started, 1 Needs review, 1 Learning; Berlin = 9 Not started, 1 Needs review; all other groups entirely Not started. Legend behavior is specified separately below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
